Z||000000||TylerB11||10-23-2001||03:09 PM||||I was driving today and suddenly my GT is acting weird, it is hesitating heavily when I step on the gas, and when i pull over, it struggles and dies. Now it won't start. It rotates fine, but just won't or barely turn over.<BR>I checked:<BR>Gas- plenty of it, I can hear the fuel pump on for 2 secs and then comes back on as I rotate the engine. I also checked the fuel pressure release valve on the engine, and there was fuel pressure.<BR>Spark - I pulled a plug - it was dry. I hooked it back up and rotated the engine again. it sparked, but it was a reddish-white spark that looked kinda weak.<P>Any ideas?<BR>I am away at school, so my tools are kind of limited.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||03:13 PM||||Could be the ignition module in the distributor, Or if it is not getting gas the fuel pump may have went south.<P>Good Luck<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||beer_stud_21||10-23-2001||03:48 PM||||When you say "but just won't or barely turn over." do you mean it won't turn over, or won't fire?  Put your foot to the floor and turn it over for 20 sec or so.  If it at least sputters your getting at least a little bit of gas.  If not pull the plug and see if its dry or not.  Have you replaced your fuel filter recently?  <P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000003||TylerB11||10-23-2001||05:12 PM||||It seems to be getting gas to the MPFI - there is pressure at the schrader valve on the fuel rail. Once I release the pressure, and turn it over, it regains pressure at the valve.<BR>But the plugs aren't all fouled- they are dry as a bone.<P>I tried resetting the ECM and cleaning the battery contacts as per haynes.<P>i can hear the FP and it sounds fine.<P>Could it be an MPFI problem? Whats the easiest way to check that and the coil?<P><BR>Thanks all!<P>EDIT: it does fire a little at the begining - sputtering. <p>[This message has been edited by TylerB11 (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||05:16 PM||||I know that most parts stores can check the ignition module for free.  Check the ECM and injector fuses in the box. ||||reg||3
Z||000005||Gary W||10-23-2001||09:18 PM||||If I read the service manual flowchart right, you can disconnect the 4-wire connector to the ignition module at the base of the distributor. If the engine now starts, the pickup coil is bad. Gotta pull the distributor to change it, but it's a $10 part. (You cant drive it like this, it's just a component test)||||reg||1
Z||000006||TylerB11||10-23-2001||10:26 PM||||Gary - tried that - no dice.<P>I'm back to thinking its fuel related. It sputters when i first turn the key over, then nothing. I can hear the fuel pump the whole time...turn key, 2 secs of FP. attempt to start - hear FP going... stop trying to start - hear FP for another 3 seconds, then stop. There is pressure at the valve on the fuel rail. hmm....||||reg||1
Z||000007||Indiana_resto_guy||10-24-2001||12:50 AM||||Have you checked the injector connector and fuses?<P>With the plugs being dry, pressure at the valve = no fuel being delivered.<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 10-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||TylerB11||10-24-2001||11:18 AM||||Yeah, the fuses are fine. The reason I don't think it is the injectors is because it starts to fire when you first turn the key, then nothing.||||reg||1
